WEBVTT

00:00:00.333 --> 00:00:02.863
Is the Moon really
changing shape every night?

00:00:03.129 --> 00:00:03.639
No.

00:00:03.989 --> 00:00:06.039
The Moon never changes shape at all.

00:00:06.255 --> 00:00:08.505
Half of the Moon is always lit by the sun.

00:00:08.796 --> 00:00:12.046
What changes is how much of
that bright half we can see.

00:00:12.317 --> 00:00:14.487
The Moon travels around Earth in an orbit.

00:00:14.812 --> 00:00:18.522
When it is between us and the sun,
its lit side faces away.

00:00:18.843 --> 00:00:19.813
That is a new moon.

00:00:20.199 --> 00:00:22.529
A few days later, we see a thin crescent.

00:00:22.834 --> 00:00:25.784
About a week in, we see half of it,
called the first quarter.

00:00:26.175 --> 00:00:30.345
When the Moon is on the far side of Earth,
the whole lit face points to us.

00:00:30.601 --> 00:00:31.611
That is a full moon.

00:00:31.997 --> 00:00:36.107
Then it shrinks back to new, in a cycle
of about twenty-nine and a half days.

00:00:36.477 --> 00:00:39.247
Many people think the phases
come from Earth's shadow.

00:00:39.623 --> 00:00:40.493
They do not.

00:00:40.804 --> 00:00:43.194
Earth's shadow only
causes a lunar eclipse.

00:00:43.489 --> 00:00:46.679
The Moon also spins once
for every trip around Earth.

00:00:46.990 --> 00:00:49.720
That is why we always see
the same face of the Moon.

00:00:50.036 --> 00:00:51.546
The far side is not dark.

00:00:51.871 --> 00:00:53.121
It gets sunlight too.

00:00:53.397 --> 00:00:54.607
So tonight, look up.

00:00:54.898 --> 00:00:57.908
You are watching light and orbit,
not a changing moon.

